  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For an array BBB containing MMM non-negative integers, we define f(B)f(B)f(B) to be the number of distinct values among its prefix bitwise ORs.\n\nFormally, let PPP be an array of length MMM, such that:\n\n\nP1=B1P_1 = B_1P1​=B1​\nPi=Bi&nbsp;∣&nbsp;Pi−1P_i = B_i \\ \\mid\\ P_{i-1}Pi​=Bi​&nbsp;∣&nbsp;Pi−1​ for each 1&lt;i≤M1 \\lt i \\leq M1&lt;i≤M.\n\nHere ∣\\mid∣ denotes the bitwise OR operation.\nf(B)f(B)f(B) is then defined to be the number of distinct elements in PPP.\n\nYou are given an array AAA consisting of NNN integers, satisfying 0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N0≤Ai​≤N.\n\nFind the maximum possible value of f(A)f(A)f(A) across all rearrangements of AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line contains a single integer TTT — the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the size of the array.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array AAA.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output a single integer — the maximum value of f(A)f(A)f(A) across all rearrangements of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "1≤N≤2×1051 \\leq N \\leq 2 \\times 10^51≤N≤2×105",
      "0≤Ai≤N0 \\leq A_i \\leq N0≤Ai​≤N",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2×1052 \\times 10^52×105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n3\n3 2 1\n7\n0 3 5 4 7 0 6",
        "output": "2\n4",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: Let's look at all rearrangements of AAA.\n\n[3,2,1][3, 2, 1][3,2,1]: the prefix OR array is [3,3,3][3, 3, 3][3,3,3], with one distinct element.\n[3,1,2][3, 1, 2][3,1,2]: the prefix OR array is [3,3,3][3, 3, 3][3,3,3], with one distinct element.\n[1,2,3][1, 2, 3][1,2,3]: the prefix OR array is [1,3,3][1, 3, 3][1,3,3], with two distinct elements.\n[1,3,2][1, 3, 2][1,3,2]: the prefix OR array is [1,3,3][1, 3, 3][1,3,3], with two distinct elements.\n[2,1,3][2, 1, 3][2,1,3]: the prefix OR array is [2,3,3][2, 3, 3][2,3,3], with two distinct elements.\n[2,3,1][2, 3, 1][2,3,1]: the prefix OR array is [2,3,3][2, 3, 3][2,3,3], with two distinct elements.\n\nThe maximum number of distinct prefix ORs across all rearrangements is hence 222."
      }
